---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: superpowers-docs-governance
root: true
purpose: >
  Specs and plans — the authored design surface. Born-linked, decomposes to gaps,
  graduates to history; never parked. See the framing spec for the full law.
rules:
  - id: doc-frontmatter-at-birth
    class: deny
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    require-frontmatter: [id, status, cites]
    why: "No doc born without id + status + cites (the .epr-meta law)."
    retire-when: "when doc frontmatter is GENERATED at creation by the scaffolding path (cite-gen minting id/status/cites) rather than hand-authored — a doc without it becomes unconstructible, and a gate against an unconstructible shape is dead weight"
  - id: ssr-doorway-boundary
    class: ask
    when: { write: "*ssr*.md", contains-any: ["doorway"], new: true }
    dedupe-of: genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-render-delivery-manifest-adapter-design.md
    why: "Doorway is a projector, never a render dependency — the renderer is an optional feature of the peer runtime (storage `ssr` feature), and a zero-doorway mesh must retain full SSR delivery. The boundary is settled in the render-delivery adapter spec §3e; frame the serving side as 'serving peer' and cite that spec rather than re-deriving doorway-as-SSR-dependency."
    retire-when: "when the render-delivery adapter spec §3e is cited by every live SSR doc and the boundary has gone two consecutive quarters without being re-derived — a settled boundary nobody re-opens needs no teacher"
  - id: render-doorway-boundary
    class: ask
    when: { write: "*render*.md", contains-any: ["doorway"], new: true }
    dedupe-of: genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-render-delivery-manifest-adapter-design.md
    why: "Doorway is a projector, never a render dependency — the renderer is an optional feature of the peer runtime (storage `ssr` feature), and a zero-doorway mesh must retain full SSR delivery. The boundary is settled in the render-delivery adapter spec §3e; frame the serving side as 'serving peer' and cite that spec rather than re-deriving doorway-as-SSR-dependency."
    retire-when: "same condition as ssr-doorway-boundary, and they should retire together — two `when` patterns over one settled boundary, not two boundaries"
validators: []
max-cascade-depth: 8
cites:
  - 2026-06-25-doc-lifecycle-as-epr-development-substrate-design
---

# superpowers/ — authored design surface

The base governance for specs and plans. Child `.epr-meta` files tighten this per-directory.
